From 459d766885e59442f4242bf85474721ea43b58ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:45:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ipq40xx: w-118: pin the LAN bridge MAC to the label MAC

The port keeps the uplink and LAN 1-3 in one LAN bridge, as an AP
uses its uplink. The uplink carries the label MAC (ART 0x0, the one
Arista uses) and LAN 1-3 the gmac's (ART 0x6). With no MAC set,
netifd gives the bridge the MAC of the first member present when it
sets the bridge up, in name order: the uplink at boot, lan1 after a
later reload. So br-lan went from 88:b1:e1:03:16:1f to ...:1e on a
network reload with the same config. Set the LAN MAC to the label MAC
in board.d, as google,wifi does for its WAN.

B111: board.d run into a temporary board.json gives lan macaddr
88:b1:e1:03:16:1f; with that macaddr on its br-lan, the W-118 kept the
label MAC and its DHCP lease across a reload and a restart.

Upstream #26028 doesn't need it: there the uplink is the WAN and
LAN 1-3 alone form the LAN.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network b/target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
index f0f0566f3f..95aa83d689 100644
--- a/target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
+++ b/target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
@@ -192,6 +192,9 @@ ipq40xx_setup_macs()
 	local label_mac=""
 
 	case "$board" in
+	arista,w-118)
+		lan_mac=$(get_mac_label)
+		;;
 	avm,fritzbox-7530)
 		local tffsdev=$(find_mtd_chardev "nand-tffs")
 		wan_mac=$(/usr/bin/fritz_tffs_nand -b -d $tffsdev -n macdsl)
-- 
